\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ce64b70c501362dc8d69c623fbd67059e5eecc1885fbb26687990b7ac3c2a5b2","event_uuid":"229605e5-c050-40de-abcc-d7f012fee5a0","position":{"commit_sha":"14ae577dde38658fce83af54f9f6b1425e06a243","position":"1788898185978322001-229605e5-c050-40de-abcc-d7f012fee5a0"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"7026068d725e7dc824c0421b7a51d084e77c4e912b60d41cbe2ca5d3cbd90506","event_uuid":"00916a96-f23d-44aa-91c7-f2c44ed033d2","position":{"commit_sha":"48171a10c1eb007ab3574bfa34dad2e8a55352f2","position":"1788898199221309001-00916a96-f23d-44aa-91c7-f2c44ed033d2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Created from REB closeout failures. Existing prior bug ferric-jet-scorpion fixed own-or-descendant commit crediting, but ibex/goitered/wrasse still fail the deterministic close precheck after AC completion and child closeout; beginning RCA.","timestamp":1788895139377337001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RCA complete. Repro: ibex/goitered/wrasse each have complete ACs and all children closed, but close precheck fails before verifier with 'no commit references it (nor any of its descendants)'. Code path: close_precheck._completion_precheck -> _resolved_completion_scope -> _check_work_landed -> _referencing_commits. Prior fix ferric-jet-scorpion correctly unions the parent and transitive descendants, but these closeout epics' implementation children were administrative duplicate shells: each closed child records the work as living on a replacement ticket outside the parent subtree. The accepted-id set omitted those live replacement tickets, so referencing_commits scanned only duplicate shells and found zero, while the real landed commits reference the replacements. Verdict: genuine deterministic precheck defect, not intended policy. The gate should credit closed disposition replacements (and their subtree) as evidence while still failing when no referenced/attached commit exists anywhere in that expanded evidence set.","timestamp":1788897997884920001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation milestone: RED regression test_parent_close_credits_duplicate_child_replacement_commit reproduced the parent close precheck failure when the only landed commit referenced a duplicate child's live replacement. Fix expands completion evidence scope from closed disposition tickets to their live replacements and descendants, without dropping the existing no-reference fail-closed protection. Targeted validation is green: pytest close subtree + completion gate + duration instrumentation (49 passed) and ruff check on changed files passed. File impact updated to actual changed paths.","timestamp":1788898199221309001}],"created_at":1788895094276895001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6cca2083-2fe8-4501-a47a-f8feb8a104db","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"95da-0b4f-06a8-4b9c"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThree REB epic closeouts are blocked after all acceptance criteria were marked complete and their open children were closed:\n\n- `nauseating-inquiring-ibex` / `95da-0b4f-06a8-4b9c`\n- `subjective-sudden-goitered` / `df55-1305-956e-431b`\n- `decorous-plucky-wrasse` / `e867-0f39-b887-40fa`\n\nEach close fails before the completion verifier with:\n\n```text\nError: cannot close <epic>: it records file_impact (a code change) but no commit references it (nor any of its descendants). Add a 'rebar-ticket: <id>' trailer to the commit that implements it, then retry (or override with --force=\"<reason>\"). Completion verification cannot confirm the work landed without a referencing commit.\n```\n\nPrior bug `ferric-jet-scorpion` (`1edf-2261-a092-43e5`) fixed the simpler case where a parent should credit commits from its transitive descendants. This bug tracks the remaining closeout failure: coordination/rollup epics may be proven by closed children, administrative duplicate/obsolete dispositions, and replacement tickets, yet the deterministic precheck still prevents a non-force close.\n\n## RCA Plan\n\n1. Reproduce using the three blocked epics above and capture the full close-precheck error.\n2. Locate the deterministic completion precheck and referencing-commit scan in `src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py` and its tests.\n3. Trace the accepted-id set built for an epic: own id, transitive descendants, and any replacement/superseding tickets recorded by administrative close dispositions.\n4. Determine whether the failure is a defect or intended policy. If it is intended behavior requiring policy change, stop and escalate. If it is a defect, fix only the missing evidence path while preserving the fail-closed protection for code tickets with no landed/referenced work.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The bug is classified with RCA as either a genuine defect or intended policy; the ticket records the exact code path and evidence.\n- [ ] If defect, a RED test reproduces a blocked epic close where closed child/replacement evidence should satisfy the deterministic landed-work precheck.\n- [ ] The fix preserves the current protection: a code-impact ticket with no referencing commit in its accepted evidence set still fails with `cannot confirm the work landed`.\n- [ ] The three known blocked epics (`ibex`, `goitered`, `wrasse`) can close without `--force` after the fix lands, or the ticket records why a policy decision is required instead.\n- [ ] Targeted tests and `make verify` pass before Gerrit upload.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_precheck.py","reason":"Expands completion close evidence scope before landed-work/reference checks."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_scope.py","reason":"Adds narrow helper for closed disposition replacement evidence expansion."},{"path":"tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_close_gate_subtree.py","reason":"Regression coverage for parent closes crediting duplicate replacement commits."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2bf903b1-2ac7-49a7-85ed-4d5c9a916f56","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9181-7c2e-5718-4f7f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion close precheck still misses implemented descendant/replacement evidence for epic closeouts","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8582ff6e-7791-49de-ab33-68915ccb5a02","6cca2083-2fe8-4501-a47a-f8feb8a104db","81e2e10d-9826-4da2-999b-3e00378fffb0","5c65c56e-4a0f-4bd8-966d-269f07e4b699","9d185451-dda9-49b8-9542-201f9fac91f5","2bf903b1-2ac7-49a7-85ed-4d5c9a916f56","2693ee75-a32e-478e-8826-084e91a45e53","602843d7-72b8-4dfb-ba5b-1a685c589ccf","229605e5-c050-40de-abcc-d7f012fee5a0","00916a96-f23d-44aa-91c7-f2c44ed033d2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788898199221309002,"uuid":"f031d49b-1b34-47da-b141-fdb960d71474"}